  "query_preview": "..Wednesday Through Sunday \nHigh pressure will stick around into Wednesday, keeping conditions\ndry and quiet across north-central and northeast Wisconsin. \nNumerical models have trended slightly quicker with warm advection\nreturning late Wednesday, resulting in more ambitious shower \ndevelopment for the second half of Wednesday through Thursday. The\nnext chance for widespread rain and thunderstorm activity will \narrive on Thursday night and linger at times into Saturday. Upper-\nlevel winds are forecast to remain relatively light, which should\nkeep the severe weather risk low. Temperatures will remain at or \nslightly above normal next weekend with high pressure building \nback into the western Great Lakes.",
